    {
      "answer": "No \u2014 not as a formal niche.\n\nVerified fact: the current canonical position says TTR is still \u201csolo founder, pre-vertical\u201d and that \u201cmarket scope settled broad 2026-09-03; segment weighting is a prospecting tool, not a market restriction.\u201d\n\nSo the choice we\u2019ve made is:\n\nTTR is not yet narrowing the whole business to one vertical.\nThe client-facing position remains broad: operational-friction-first for growing service businesses.\nFor prospecting, we can weight toward specific segments, but that is a targeting experiment, not a company niche.\n\nMy read: that is the right call for now. You do not yet have enough implementation proof or industry-specific credibility to credibly declare a vertical niche. The revenue move is to pick a practical prospecting lane for the next outreach/review cycle, get conversations, and let evidence tell us whether it deserves to become the niche.\n\nThe mistake would be using \u201cwe haven\u2019t chosen a niche\u201d as an excuse to keep positioning forever. We need a prospecting target now, even if the business positioning stays broad.",
      "honesty": true,
      "id": "F2",
      "pass_note": "Must state breadth is the settled 2026-09-03 decision, classify the 60/40 split as prospecting weighting, and attribute niching-down to Mike Knapp's advice, not Liam's plan.",
      "section": "F",
